    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and both its tests pass with a clean build.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `ownerSegment` field so that `GET /api/owners/{id}` returns it formatted `<TIER>_<AREA>`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `ownerSegment` string property to the `Owner` schema with the four-value enum (`PREMIUM_METRO`, `PREMIUM_REGIONAL`, `STANDARD_METRO`, `STANDARD_REGIONAL`). The OpenAPI generator produces `OwnerDto.OwnerSegmentEnum` from this.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../rest/function/owner/OwnerSegment.java`** (new) \u2014 `OwnerSegment.of(Owner)` derives the segment:\n   - **TIER**: `PREMIUM` when the effective membership level (stored value, else `MembershipLevel.of(owner)` \u2014 matching how the mapper computes `membershipLevel`) is \u2265 3, else `STANDARD`.\n   - **AREA**: `METRO` when the locality (region component of the customer code) is a known region (NSW/VIC/QLD), else `REGIONAL`. Known-region detection reuses `Locality.timezone(region)` being non-null, which is exactly NSW/VIC/QLD.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` for `ownerSegment` wrapping the helper in `OwnerDto.OwnerSegmentEnum.fromValue(...)`, following the existing `contactPreference` pattern.\n\nThe two acceptance tests (`STANDARD_METRO` for a known Sydney/NSW owner, `STANDARD_REGIONAL` for an unknown city) and the full build pass green.",
